Krita Nova 70 - Selection tools: Shift switches freehand <-> polygon

- Tool Invocation: while a selection tool is active, a shortcut that
  switches to a temporary tool (Activate Line Tool, Ellipse, Rectangle,
  Move, Fill, Gradient, Measure, the selection tools...) does not switch:
  the press goes to the selection tool, where Shift held when the
  selection starts means Add to selection, as in Krita.
- Freehand Selection: pressing Shift while drawing switches to straight
  segments (polygon): a straight line follows the cursor; lifting the pen
  with Shift held leaves a corner there and further clicks add corners;
  letting go of Shift with the pen down goes on drawing freehand from there,
  with the pen up it finishes the selection (as letting go of Ctrl in
  Krita's continued mode does).
- Polygonal Selection: while the polygon is being drawn, Shift held makes
  a drag draw freehand, until Shift is let go.
(KisToolOutlineBase::setShiftSwitchesToPolygon,
KisToolPolylineBase::setShiftSwitchesToFreehand; only these two tools turn
them on.)

